# CASP15 T1158v4 — The Engine Room (8SWN)
---

Every pump needs fuel.

This is MRP4 bound to ATP — adenosine triphosphate —
the universal energy currency of life.

This structure shows the engine that powers
the prostaglandin pump.

> close
> load 8swn
---

ABC transporters like MRP4 have two nucleotide-
binding domains that sandwich ATP between them.

When ATP is hydrolyzed, the energy released
drives a conformational change that pushes
the cargo through the membrane.

> spin 0.15
---

Here's the ATP binding site — the engine room
of this molecular machine.

This is a fundamentally different prediction
challenge from the prostaglandin binding sites.
ATP binds in a conserved pocket shared
across thousands of proteins.

> stop
> view ligand
---

Four structures of the same protein,
four completely different ligands,
four different prediction challenges.

This is what made the MRP4 targets
such a comprehensive test of docking methods.

> reset
> spin 0.1
---

MRP4 with ATP — fuel for the pump.
PDB code 8SWN, CASP15 target T1158v4.

> stop
